HOW THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS REACH A USER
=======================================

Everything under src/, scripts/, tests/, docs/, and notebooks/ is the work of
Ecodylic Science unless a module docstring says otherwise. Mosaic bundles no
third-party source code and no trained model weights.

The components below reach a user in one of four ways, and which one decides
what that user owes:

  invoked        A separate program that mosaic starts and talks to over a
                 pipe, a socket, or the filesystem. Mosaic does not link it,
                 import it, or ship it; the user installs it independently.

  optional       A Python distribution named in an optional extra in
                 pyproject.toml. Installing mosaic-behavior does not install
                 it. Asking for the extra makes pip fetch it from its own
                 publisher, under that publisher's license.

  fetched        Model weights that a component downloads from a model hub
                 the first time it runs. Nothing is fetched at install time,
                 nothing is redistributed here, and the terms are the ones
                 the hub entry states at the moment of download.

Two components carry restrictions that the AGPL does not, and both are called
out below: keypoint-MoSeq prohibits commercial use outright, and TRex requires
a paid license for company use.


