THE REST OF THE DEPENDENCY GRAPH
================================

The remaining runtime and development dependencies are permissively licensed
(BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0, PSF). The NVIDIA CUDA runtime libraries that arrive
with GPU builds of PyTorch are proprietary but commercially redistributable
under NVIDIA's own terms; they are not open source and not non-commercial.

The resolved set is recorded in uv.lock, and

    python scripts/gen_third_party_inventory.py

regenerates the full inventory from it: per extra and per dependency group,
the transitive closure with each distribution's license resolved from PyPI
metadata and flagged when it is not permissive. It reads the isolated
keypoint-MoSeq lock as well. No count is written down in this file, because a
written count goes stale silently; the script emits its own.
